# Fixture: GRUB already carries a MANAGED GPU id that lspci no longer reports
# (10de:2330 — an H100 this playbook knows about), i.e. a hot-removed or wedged
# device. Writing the freshly discovered — shorter — list would unbind it on the
# next boot, so the role must REFUSE.
#
# The id has to be one of lium_cc_gpu_pci_ids / lium_nvswitch_pci_ids. An id
# outside that set is never looked for in lspci, so its absence proves nothing
# and is not a narrowing at all — see the unmanaged_id fixture.
GRUB_DEFAULT=0
GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX="kvm_intel.tdx=on vfio-pci.ids=10de:2335,10de:22a3,10de:2330"
GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT="intel_iommu=on iommu=pt nohibernate"
